-----------------------------------------------------------------------------



             Setup commands used in the BBS:ACCESSLEVEL/LEVEL_(n)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

ACCLEVEL                 (pn)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : Select accesslevel for user

CONFJOIN                 (pt)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : Select a default conference for user to join
                                  when this accesslevel is loaded.
                                  This function is only in use, when the 
                                  accounts for a newuser and guest is used.

CHATDAYLIMIT             (pn)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : Select a daily chat limit for user

DLDAYLIMIT               (pn)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : Select maximum download bytes per day.

DOWNLOADFILES            (pn)   : DEFAULT: 0
                                : select number of files user will start
                                  to have downloaded.

DOWNLOADBYTES            (pn)   : DEFAULT: 0
                                : select number of bytes user will start
                                  to have uploaded.

RATIO                    (pn)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : Select RATIO for current usertype.

RATIOTYPE                (pt)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : Select RATIOTYPE for usertype.
                                  You can choose between 4 different ratiotypes
                                  for a user:
                                   DISABLED      : User got freedown
                                                   He do not need to upload
                                                   before download

                                   BYTES         : Users upload bytes
                                                   will be compared using
                                                   selected ratio and
                                                   if he do not have enough
                                                   bytes left, he will not
                                                   be able to download.

                                   FILES         : Users upload files
                                                   will be compared using
                                                   selected ratio and
                                                   if he do not have enough
                                                   files left, he will not
                                                   be able to download.

                                   FILES&BYTES   : User got both file and
                                                   byte ratio, both will be
                                                   checked when he tries to
                                                   download.

TIMEDAYLIMIT             (pn)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : Select a daily timelimit for user

USERTYPE                 (pt)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : Select a usertype for user

UPLOADFILES              (pn)   : DEFAULT: 0
                                : select number of files user will start
                                  to have uploaded.

UPLOADBYTES              (pn)   : DEFAULT: 0
                                : select number of bytes user will start
                                  to have uploaded.

